<<<
+ lish k&’na-an; k&a’na-an into ka’nayan, & that into kA‘nyan; the pronunciation k&’nan, alone recognized by the OED, but chiefly in clerical use, is a worse evasion of the same difficulty.
===
+ lish kă *na-an*; kă *na-an* passes into kă'*nayan*, & that into kă'*nyan*; the pronunciation kă'*nan*, alone recognized by the OED, but chiefly in clerical use, is a worse evasion of the same difficulty.
>>>

