<<<
cantatrice is usually pronounced as Italian (-Echa), sometimes as French (-€s); singer should be preferred when it is not misleading; other English substitutes, as songstress, (ene singer, are seldom tolerable;

ut see FEMININE DESIGNATIONS.
===
**cantatrice** is usually pronounced as Italian (-ēchā), sometimes as French (-ēs); *singer* should be preferred when it is not misleading; other English substitutes, as *songstress*, *female singer*, are seldom tolerable; but see ^^FEMININE DESIGNATIONS^^.
>>>

